# 必考词 Unit13
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2025红宝书考研英语词汇
# 描述: 必考词Unit13核心词汇

{{bachelor}}{{/ˈbætʃələr}}{{n. 学士；单身汉；未婚男子}}{{He earned a bachelor's degree in computer science.}}
{{bail}}{{/beɪl}}{{n./v. 保释；保释金；舀水；跳伞}}{{The suspect was released on bail.}}
{{ban}}{{/bæn}}{{v./n. 禁止；禁令；取缔；谴责}}{{The government imposed a ban on smoking in public places.}}
{{bankrupt}}{{/ˈbæŋkrʌpt}}{{adj./v. 破产的；使破产；完全缺乏的}}{{The company went bankrupt due to poor management.}}
{{barely}}{{/ˈbeəli}}{{adv. 仅仅；几乎不；勉强；刚好}}{{He barely passed the exam.}}
{{barrier}}{{/ˈbæriər}}{{n. 障碍；屏障；关口；壁垒}}{{Language can be a barrier to communication.}}
{{batch}}{{/bætʃ}}{{n. 一批；一组；一批生产量；一次烘烤量}}{{The first batch of products was sold out quickly.}}
{{beam}}{{/biːm}}{{n./v. 光束；横梁；笑容；发射；广播}}{{She beamed with joy when she heard the news.}}
{{behalf}}{{/bɪˈhɑːf}}{{n. 代表；利益；方面；支持}}{{I am writing on behalf of the entire team.}}
{{behavio(u)r}}{{/bɪˈheɪvjər}}{{n. 行为；举止；表现；态度；习性}}{{The child's behavior has improved significantly.}}
{{beneficial}}{{/ˌbenɪˈfɪʃl}}{{adj. 有益的；有利的；有帮助的；有好处的}}{{Regular exercise is beneficial to health.}}
{{benefit}}{{/ˈbenɪfɪt}}{{n./v. 好处；受益；利益；津贴；义演}}{{Regular exercise has many health benefits.}}
{{betray}}{{/bɪˈtreɪ}}{{v. 背叛；泄露；辜负；暴露；出卖}}{{He felt betrayed by his closest friend.}}
{{bias}}{{/ˈbaɪəs}}{{n./v. 偏见；偏向；偏差；倾向性；斜裁}}{{The report was criticized for its political bias.}}
{{bind}}{{/baɪnd}}{{v. 捆绑；约束；装订；使结合；使负有义务}}{{The contract binds both parties to the agreement.}}
{{blaze}}{{/bleɪz}}{{n./v. 火焰；燃烧；闪耀；光辉；迸发}}{{The fire blazed throughout the night.}}
{{blend}}{{/blend}}{{v./n. 混合；融合；混合物；调和；交融}}{{The coffee blend has a unique flavor.}}
{{block}}{{/blɒk}}{{n./v. 街区；阻塞；障碍；大楼；一组}}{{The fallen tree blocked the road.}}
{{bloom}}{{/bluːm}}{{v./n. 开花；繁盛；花期；青春；红润}}{{The flowers bloom beautifully in spring.}}
{{blunder}}{{/ˈblʌndər}}{{n./v. 大错；犯大错；失误；跟跄}}{{The company made a blunder by ignoring customer feedback.}}
{{blunt}}{{/blʌnt}}{{adj./v. 钝的；直率的；使变钝；迟钝的}}{{He is known for his blunt manner of speaking.}}
{{boast}}{{/bəʊst}}{{v./n. 自夸；夸耀；拥有；引以为豪的东西}}{{He boasted about his achievements to everyone.}}
{{bold}}{{/bəʊld}}{{adj. 大胆的；醒目的；冒失的；黑体的}}{{She made a bold decision to start her own business.}}
{{bond}}{{/bɒnd}}{{n./v. 纽带；联系；结合；债券；约束}}{{The mother and child share a strong emotional bond.}}
{{boom}}{{/buːm}}{{n./v. 繁荣；隆隆声；暴涨；迅速发展}}{{The tech industry experienced a boom in the 2000s.}}
{{boost}}{{/buːst}}{{v./n. 促进；增加；推动；提高；增强}}{{The new policy will boost the economy.}}
{{brace}}{{/breɪs}}{{v./n. 支撑；做好准备；使振作；支架；大括号}}{{They braced themselves for the incoming storm.}}
{{brake}}{{/breɪk}}{{n./v. 刹车；制动器；阻碍；减速}}{{He hit the brakes to avoid the collision.}}
{{breach}}{{/briːtʃ}}{{n./v. 违反；缺口；突破；破坏；攻破}}{{The company was in breach of contract.}}
{{breakthrough}}{{/ˈbreɪkθruː}}{{n. 突破；重大进展；突破性成就；关键问题的解决}}{{Scientists have made a breakthrough in cancer research.}}
{{breed}}{{/briːd}}{{v./n. 繁殖；品种；培育；引起；类型}}{{This farm breeds high-quality cattle.}}
{{brief}}{{/briːf}}{{adj./n. 简短的；摘要；简报；短暂的；概要}}{{He gave a brief summary of the report.}}
{{brilliant}}{{/ˈbrɪliənt}}{{adj. 杰出的；明亮的；辉煌的；聪颖的}}{{She is a brilliant scientist with many achievements.}}
{{brisk}}{{/brɪsk}}{{adj. 活跃的；兴隆的；凉爽的；轻快的；生气勃勃的}}{{Business has been brisk this quarter.}}
{{broad}}{{/brɔːd}}{{adj. 宽阔的；广泛的；概括的；明显的；口音重的}}{{The road is broad enough for four lanes.}}
{{browse}}{{/braʊz}}{{v. 浏览；吃草；随意翻阅；随便看看}}{{She browsed through the magazine while waiting.}}
{{bruise}}{{/bruːz}}{{n./v. 淤伤；擦伤；碰伤；挫伤；伤害}}{{He fell and bruised his knee.}}
{{budget}}{{/ˈbʌdʒɪt}}{{n./v. 预算；编预算；经费；专款；廉价的}}{{The government increased the education budget this year.}}
{{bulk}}{{/bʌlk}}{{n. 大批；大部分；体积；容量；大量}}{{The bulk of the work has been completed.}}
{{bulletin}}{{/ˈbʊlətɪn}}{{n. 公告；简报；新闻快报；学报；通报}}{{The company issued a bulletin about the new policy.}}
{{bump}}{{/bʌmp}}{{v./n. 碰撞；肿块；颠簸；撞击；隆起}}{{The car bumped into the wall.}}
{{burden}}{{/ˈbɜːdn}}{{n./v. 负担；使负重；责任；装载量；忧虑}}{{The financial burden was too heavy for the family.}}
{{bureau}}{{/ˈbjʊərəʊ}}{{n. 局；处；办公室；写字台；五斗橱}}{{The Federal Bureau of Investigation handles federal crimes.}}
{{burst}}{{/bɜːst}}{{v./n. 爆裂；突然发生；爆发；冲刺；一阵}}{{The balloon burst when he sat on it.}}
{{bypass}}{{/ˈbaɪpɑːs}}{{v./n. 绕过；旁路；绕道；忽视；回避}}{{We took the bypass to avoid the traffic jam.}}
{{calculate}}{{/ˈkælkjuleɪt}}{{v. 计算；估计；推测；打算；指望}}{{Scientists calculated the distance between the two stars.}}
{{campaign}}{{/kæmˈpeɪn}}{{n./v. 运动；战役；竞选活动；参加竞选；作战}}{{The marketing campaign was a huge success.}}
{{candidate}}{{/ˈkændɪdət}}{{n. 候选人；应试者；求职者；报考者}}{{There are five candidates for the position.}}
{{capacity}}{{/kəˈpæsəti}}{{n. 能力；容量；身份；职位；生产力}}{{The stadium has a capacity of 50,000 spectators.}}
{{capsule}}{{/ˈkæpsjuːl}}{{n. 胶囊；太空舱；小容器；摘要；密封舱}}{{The medicine comes in capsule form.}}
{{capture}}{{/ˈkæptʃər}}{{v./n. 捕获；夺取；吸引；拍摄；战利品}}{{The photographer captured a beautiful sunset.}}
{{casual}}{{/ˈkæʒuəl}}{{adj. 随便的；偶然的；非正式的；不经意的}}{{He wore casual clothes to the party.}}
{{catalogue}}{{/ˈkætəlɒɡ}}{{n. 目录；一览表；系列；登记；编目}}{{You can browse the product catalogue online.}}
{{catastrophe}}{{/kəˈtæstrəfi}}{{n. 灾难；大祸；惨败；严重的不幸}}{{The oil spill was an environmental catastrophe.}}
{{category}}{{/ˈkætəɡəri}}{{n. 种类；类别；范畴；类型；等级}}{{The books are arranged by category in the library.}}
{{cease}}{{/siːs}}{{v. 停止；终止；结束；中断；不再}}{{The factory ceased production due to lack of raw materials.}}
{{ceremony}}{{/ˈserəməni}}{{n. 典礼；仪式；礼节；礼仪；客套}}{{The opening ceremony of the Olympics was spectacular.}}
{{certificate}}{{/sərˈtɪfɪkət}}{{n. 证书；证明；凭证；文凭；合格证}}{{She received a certificate for completing the course.}}
{{challenge}}{{/ˈtʃælɪndʒ}}{{n./v. 挑战；质疑；怀疑；艰巨任务；邀请比赛}}{{Learning a new language is always a challenge.}}
{{champion}}{{/ˈtʃæmpiən}}{{n. 冠军；拥护者；斗士；捍卫者}}{{She became the world champion in swimming.}}
{{channel}}{{/ˈtʃænl}}{{n. 频道；渠道；海峡；途径；通道}}{{The English Channel separates England from France.}}
{{chaos}}{{/ˈkeɪɒs}}{{n. 混乱；无秩序；混沌；纷乱}}{{The earthquake left the city in chaos.}}
{{characteristic}}{{/ˌkærəktəˈrɪstɪk}}{{n./adj. 特征；特有的；典型的；独特的}}{{Kindness is one of her most admirable characteristics.}}
{{charter}}{{/ˈtʃɑːtər}}{{n./v. 宪章；包租；特许状；许可证；租用}}{{The company chartered a plane for the trip.}}
{{chronic}}{{/ˈkrɒnɪk}}{{adj. 慢性的；长期的；习惯性的；严重的}}{{He suffers from chronic back pain.}}
{{circulate}}{{/ˈsɜːkjəleɪt}}{{v. 循环；流通；传播；流传；散布}}{{Blood circulates through the body continuously.}}
{{circumstance}}{{/ˈsɜːkəmstəns}}{{n. 环境；情况；境遇；形势；状况}}{{Under no circumstance should you give up.}}
{{cite}}{{/saɪt}}{{v. 引用；举例；引证；表彰；传唤}}{{He cited several examples to support his argument.}}
{{claim}}{{/kleɪm}}{{v./n. 声称；索赔；要求；主张；断言}}{{He claims to have seen a UFO.}}
{{clarify}}{{/ˈklærɪfaɪ}}{{v. 澄清；阐明；净化；使明晰}}{{Could you clarify what you mean by that statement?}}
{{clash}}{{/klæʃ}}{{v./n. 冲突；碰撞；争论；不协调；交锋}}{{The two groups clashed over the issue.}}
{{classify}}{{/ˈklæsɪfaɪ}}{{v. 分类；归类；划分；分级；列为保密}}{{The books are classified by subject in the library.}}
{{clause}}{{/klɔːz}}{{n. 条款；从句；分句；项目；款项}}{{Please read the terms and clause carefully before signing.}}
{{climate}}{{/ˈklaɪmət}}{{n. 气候；风气；环境；氛围；趋势}}{{Climate change is one of the biggest challenges of our time.}}
{{cling}}{{/klɪŋ}}{{v. 紧抓；附着；坚持；紧贴；依恋}}{{The child clung to her mother's hand.}}
{{clinical}}{{/ˈklɪnɪkl}}{{adj. 临床的；冷静客观的；简朴的；诊所的}}{{The clinical trial showed promising results.}}
{{cluster}}{{/ˈklʌstər}}{{n./v. 群；簇；聚集；集中；一串}}{{A cluster of stars was visible in the night sky.}}
{{coalition}}{{/ˌkəʊəˈlɪʃn}}{{n. 联盟；联合；结合；同盟；联合政府}}{{The two parties formed a coalition government.}}
{{coincide}}{{/ˌkəʊɪnˈsaɪd}}{{v. 同时发生；一致；巧合；相符；重合}}{{The two events coincided by pure chance.}}
{{collaborate}}{{/kəˈlæbəreɪt}}{{v. 合作；协作；通敌；勾结；协力}}{{The two companies collaborated on the research project.}}
{{collapse}}{{/kəˈlæps}}{{v./n. 倒塌；崩溃；瓦解；病倒；折叠}}{{The building collapsed during the earthquake.}}
{{colleague}}{{/ˈkɒliːɡ}}{{n. 同事；同僚；同行；同仁}}{{She gets along well with her colleagues at work.}}
{{colony}}{{/ˈkɒləni}}{{n. 殖民地；群落；侨民区；聚居区；菌落}}{{The country was once a British colony.}}
{{combat}}{{/ˈkɒmbæt}}{{n./v. 战斗；与…斗争；格斗；搏斗；防止}}{{The government is taking measures to combat corruption.}}
{{combine}}{{/kəmˈbaɪn}}{{v. 结合；联合；兼备；组合；合并}}{{The company combined two departments to improve efficiency.}}
{{command}}{{/kəˈmɑːnd}}{{v./n. 命令；掌握；指挥；控制；俯瞰}}{{The general commanded his troops to advance.}}
{{commemorate}}{{/kəˈmeməreɪt}}{{v. 纪念；庆祝；缅怀；表彰}}{{The monument commemorates the soldiers who died in the war.}}
{{commence}}{{/kəˈmens}}{{v. 开始；着手；获得学位；开始生效}}{{The ceremony will commence at 9 a.m.}}
{{commission}}{{/kəˈmɪʃn}}{{n./v. 委员会；佣金；委托；任命；犯（罪）}}{{The artist received a commission to paint a portrait.}}
{{commit}}{{/kəˈmɪt}}{{v. 犯(罪)；承诺；投入；委托；使承诺}}{{He committed himself to finishing the project on time.}}
{{committee}}{{/kəˈmɪti}}{{n. 委员会；全体委员}}{{The committee meets every Monday to discuss policy.}}
{{commodity}}{{/kəˈmɒdəti}}{{n. 商品；日用品；有用的东西；农产品}}{{Oil is one of the most important commodities in the world.}}
{{communal}}{{/ˈkɒmjuːnl}}{{adj. 公共的；社区的；共有的；集体的； communal}}{{The garden is a communal space for all residents.}}
{{communicate}}{{/kəˈmjuːnɪkeɪt}}{{v. 交流；传达；沟通；传染；相连}}{{It is important to communicate effectively with your team.}}
{{community}}{{/kəˈmjuːnəti}}{{n. 社区；群体；共同体；社会；公众}}{{The local community organized a charity event.}}
{{compact}}{{/kəmˈpækt}}{{adj./v. 紧凑的；压缩；契约；小巧的；简洁的}}{{The apartment is compact but functional.}}
{{companion}}{{/kəmˈpæniən}}{{n. 同伴；伙伴；指南；手册；陪护}}{{The dog has been her faithful companion for years.}}
{{comparable}}{{/ˈkɒmpərəbl}}{{adj. 可比较的；类似的；比得上的；相当的}}{{The two products are comparable in quality.}}
{{comparison}}{{/kəmˈpærɪsn}}{{n. 比较；对照；比喻；类似；对比}}{{In comparison with last year, sales have increased.}}
{{compatible}}{{/kəmˈpætəbl}}{{adj. 兼容的；合得来的；可共存的；一致的}}{{The new software is compatible with most computers.}}
{{compel}}{{/kəmˈpel}}{{v. 迫使；强迫；引起；驱使；逼迫}}{{The evidence compelled him to change his mind.}}
{{compensate}}{{/ˈkɒmpenseɪt}}{{v. 补偿；赔偿；酬报；弥补；抵消}}{{The company compensated the workers for their overtime.}}
{{compete}}{{/kəmˈpiːt}}{{v. 竞争；比赛；对抗；匹敌；参加比赛}}{{Several companies are competing for the contract.}}
{{competent}}{{/ˈkɒmpɪtənt}}{{adj. 有能力的；胜任的；合格的；足够的}}{{She is a competent manager with years of experience.}}
{{compile}}{{/kəmˈpaɪl}}{{v. 编辑；汇编；收集；编制；编译}}{{The researcher compiled data from various sources.}}
{{complain}}{{/kəmˈpleɪn}}{{v. 抱怨；投诉；诉苦；申诉；发牢骚}}{{Customers complained about the poor service.}}
{{complement}}{{/ˈkɒmplɪmənt}}{{v./n. 补充；补足；补语；配对物；全套}}{{The two colors complement each other perfectly.}}
{{complex}}{{/ˈkɒmpleks}}{{adj./n. 复杂的；综合体；建筑群；情结；复合体}}{{The issue is more complex than it appears.}}
{{complicated}}{{/ˈkɒmplɪkeɪtɪd}}{{adj. 复杂的；难懂的；麻烦的；纠结的}}{{The instructions were too complicated to follow.}}
{{comply}}{{/kəmˈplaɪ}}{{v. 遵守；服从；顺从；依从；应允}}{{All employees must comply with the company policy.}}
{{component}}{{/kəmˈpəʊnənt}}{{n. 成分；部件；零件；组成部分；要素}}{{Each component of the machine must be checked regularly.}}
{{compose}}{{/kəmˈpəʊz}}{{v. 组成；创作；使镇定；作曲；排版}}{{The team is composed of experts from various fields.}}
{{comprehensive}}{{/ˌkɒmprɪˈhensɪv}}{{adj. 全面的；综合的；广泛的；有理解力的}}{{The report provides a comprehensive analysis of the situation.}}
{{comprise}}{{/kəmˈpraɪz}}{{v. 包含；由…组成；构成；包括；由…组成}}{{The committee comprises ten members.}}
{{compromise}}{{/ˈkɒmprəmaɪz}}{{n./v. 妥协；折中；和解；危害；让步}}{{Both sides reached a compromise after long negotiations.}}
{{compulsory}}{{/kəmˈpʌlsəri}}{{adj. 强制的；必修的；义务的；规定的}}{{Mathematics is a compulsory subject in schools.}}
{{conceal}}{{/kənˈsiːl}}{{v. 隐藏；隐瞒； concealment； concealment；遮住}}{{He tried to conceal his emotions.}}
{{conceive}}{{/kənˈsiːv}}{{v. 构想；怀孕；认为；想象；设想}}{{She conceived a plan to improve efficiency.}}
{{concentrate}}{{/ˈkɒnsntreɪt}}{{v. 集中；浓缩；聚集；全神贯注；富集}}{{I need to concentrate on my studies without distractions.}}
{{concept}}{{/ˈkɒnsept}}{{n. 概念；观念；想法；思想；原理}}{{The concept of freedom means different things to different people.}}
{{concern}}{{/kənˈsɜːn}}{{v./n. 关心；担忧；涉及；利害关系；公司}}{{Environmental pollution is a growing concern worldwide.}}
{{conclude}}{{/kənˈkluːd}}{{v. 结束；得出结论；推断；缔结；决定}}{{The study concluded that exercise improves mental health.}}
{{concrete}}{{/ˈkɒŋkriːt}}{{adj./n. 具体的；混凝土；实在的；有形的}}{{Please provide concrete evidence to support your claim.}}
{{condemn}}{{/kənˈdem}}{{v. 谴责；判刑；使陷入；宣告…不适用；迫使}}{{The government condemned the terrorist attack.}}
{{conduct}}{{/kənˈdʌkt}}{{v./n. 进行；行为；指挥；带领；导电}}{{The scientist conducted an important experiment.}}
{{confer}}{{/kənˈfɜːr}}{{v. 授予；协商；讨论；商议；赋予}}{{The university conferred an honorary degree on her.}}
{{confess}}{{/kənˈfes}}{{v. 承认；坦白；忏悔；供认；表明信仰}}{{He confessed that he had lied about his qualifications.}}
{{confidence}}{{/ˈkɒnfɪdəns}}{{n. 信心；信任；秘密；把握；自信}}{{She spoke with confidence during the presentation.}}
{{confine}}{{/kənˈfaɪn}}{{v. 限制；禁闭；范围；监禁；局限于}}{{The discussion was confined to the main topic.}}
{{confirm}}{{/kənˈfɜːm}}{{v. 确认；证实；批准；使坚定；使巩固}}{{The hotel confirmed our reservation by email.}}
{{conflict}}{{/ˈkɒnflɪkt}}{{n./v. 冲突；矛盾；争执；战斗；抵触}}{{The conflict between the two countries lasted for years.}}
{{conform}}{{/kənˈfɔːm}}{{v. 遵守；符合；顺从；一致；适应}}{{All products must conform to safety standards.}}
{{confuse}}{{/kənˈfjuːz}}{{v. 使困惑；混淆；使混乱；使糊涂；混同}}{{The similar names often confuse people.}}
{{congress}}{{/ˈkɒŋɡres}}{{n. 国会；代表大会；会议；聚会；协商}}{{Congress passed a new healthcare reform bill.}}
{{conjunction}}{{/kənˈdʒʌŋkʃn}}{{n. 连接；结合；连词；同时发生；联合}}{{The two events happened in conjunction with each other.}}
{{conscience}}{{/ˈkɒnʃəns}}{{n. 良心；道德心；良知；内疚；凭良心}}{{His conscience would not allow him to cheat.}}
